2026-09-06T08:56:27Z  Round 4 (Cesar: "not gripping the club properly, even less so while idle"):
  Measured: idle finger curl 0.0961 (straight) vs address 0.0412 (fist) — open hand in idle.
  Animator mask layer is a dead end (in-editor muscle clip => humanMotion=false, layer inert);
  HumanPoseHandler.SetHumanPose on finger muscles is also inert (set -0.9, curl unchanged).
  What works: bake finger bone rotations from the address frame, re-apply after the Animator.
  Idle 0.0961 -> 0.0412. Separately, the club was not INSIDE the fists — re-anchored on the fist
  centre (right fist to shaft 0.0000) and a one-bone forearm aim brings the left hand on
  (address 0.057 -> 0.017, impact 0.085 -> 0.010); declines in Idle so he carries one-handed.
  New asserts grip.rightFistOnShaft + grip.fingersClosed. 28 PASS / 1 FAIL (tri budget).
  NOTE: lost one take to my own error — two caption encodes raced on the same output and one
  deleted the raw mid-read, producing a corrupt mp4. Re-recorded serially.

2026-09-06T09:21:39Z  Round 5 (Cesar: "that is not a real golf club grip" — correct).
  Researched the real grip. Fixed two measurable defects: lead fist was -0.0057 m ABOVE the butt
  (off the end of the club) -> 0.0371 m below it; fist separation 0.058 -> 0.110 m vs one hand
  width 0.117; lead thumb was curled into a fist -> taken from the rest pose so it runs down the
  shaft. New asserts grip.leadHandOnGrip + grip.handsJoined (the in-game run CAUGHT the lead-hand
  defect at -0.0169 m, which is the harness finally measuring what Cesar can see).
  STRUCTURAL LIMIT: fingers close as a fist rather than wrapping, trail palm does not cover the
  lead thumb, no pinky overlap/interlock. Those need a hand pose AUTHORED for a club; the Mixamo
  clips are mocap with an empty hand so there is no correct grip in the data to copy.
  This is SPEC §1's anticipated fallback point. Recommendation: author one grip hand pose.

2026-09-06T09:40:54Z  Round 6: built the authored grip pose (option 1) and it CANNOT work here.
  A grip needs the wrist rolled so the knuckle line lies along the shaft. Measured at address the
  lead wrist is 58.4 deg off and the trail 69.4 deg off. The trail wrist cannot be rolled (the club
  is parented to hand_r, so it rolls with it); rolling the lead wrist swings the hand off the grip
  (fingers 0.017-0.035 -> 0.05-0.12 m short); uncapping the curl gives claws. Reverted to the best
  state. Remaining options: club-held mocap (SPEC §1 fallback, now recommended), a full arm IK
  pass, or ship the stand-in. My last-round recommendation was wrong — I scoped it as fingers when
  the wrist-to-shaft angle says wrists.

2026-09-06T09:47:49Z  Round 7: searched free mocap for club-in-hand golf.
  CMU Graphics Lab subject 64 = 30 golf trials (10 swing, 5 putt, 5 placing tee, 5 placing ball,
  5 picking up ball). Licence explicitly allows shipping inside a commercial product (no reselling
  the data). Actor demonstrably had props. CMU captures NO finger data (placeholders only) which
  is a BENEFIT here — the authored grip pose has nothing to fight, so the Mixamo failure mode
  (empty-hand fingers over un-rolled wrists) cannot recur. Bandai Namco ruled out: CC BY-NC.
  Recommendation: retarget CMU 64 + keep the authored finger pose. Motion Cast #05 is the fallback.
